+// ── F1 + F2: durable media completion ─────────────────────────────────────
+//
+// Root cause: the terminal /api/plugin/complete payload's video roles
+// (files.performance/judge1-3) were built only from in-memory
+// routineState.encodedFiles[] where uploaded&&storagePath were set, and
+// those flags were persisted to compsync-state.json ONLY *after*
+// callPluginComplete returned 2xx. A reload/restart between the video R2
+// PUT and the terminal complete wiped the in-memory association, so the
+// terminal complete (if it fired at all) carried a photo-only payload.
+//
+// F1: persist each role/photo/keyframe storagePath into durable routine
+//     state the moment its R2 PUT confirms, BEFORE the terminal complete.
+// F2: stamp a durable `videoCompletePending` marker when video roles are
+//     confirmed in R2; clear it only when the server returns a
+//     package-created status. A boot + sweep re-fire (in mediaReconciler)
+//     rebuilds the payload from the now-reliable durable state and retries.
+//
+// Server statuses that prove a media package exists for this routine, so
+// the F2 marker can safely be cleared. 'none' explicitly does NOT clear —
+// it means CompPortal has no package (the photo-only / never-fired bug).
+const PACKAGE_CREATED_STATUSES = new Set(['pending', 'processing', 'ready', 'complete', 'published'])
